    "topic": "Non-African Prose: \"Path of Lucas: The Journey He Endured\" by Susanne Bellefeuille — Background & Overview",
    "topicCode": "SS2-LIT-13",
    "module": "Non-African Prose",
    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Path of Lucas: The Journey He Endured</span> by Susanne Bellefeuille is an autobiographical Canadian novel that tells the story of Lucas Clarkson's life of sacrifice, resilience, and devotion to his family through decades of hardship.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Background of the Author</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Susanne Bellefeuille is a Canadian novelist and graduate of Social Work from St. Lawrence College in Cornwall, Ontario. She has spent years assisting people with intellectual disabilities. First published in 2017, Path of Lucas is her first novel — an autobiographical fictionalisation of her own family's story, especially the sacrifices her father made during her mother's struggle with psychotic depression.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Narrative Structure and Setting</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The novel has a non-chronological structure. It begins in the present with Lucy's car accident, then moves back into the past. Lucas, the protagonist, visits his comatose daughter Lucy in the hospital and narrates his life story to her, hoping it might help bring her out of her coma. The story oscillates between past and present, tracing Lucas's life from his teenage years to his eventual death shortly after Lucy recovers. It is set primarily in Canada and is written mostly in American/Canadian English, with some French expressions reflecting the linguistic realities of the setting.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Overview of the Story</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The novel follows Lucas Clarkson, a hardworking man whose life is shaped by devotion to his family and difficult personal choices, including giving up his dream of becoming a certified Grade A mechanic to help his father on the family farm. It portrays a story of quiet, modern heroism — marked by self-sacrifice, resilience, and enduring love — as Lucas battles the many existential forces of adult life, including his wife Isabelle's struggle with depression.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Major Themes</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Theme</th><th>Explanation</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Life as a journey</td><td>The novel frames existence as an ongoing path of struggle and growth</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Sacrifice and devotion</td><td>Lucas repeatedly gives up personal dreams for the wellbeing of his family</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Mental illness</td><td>Isabelle's struggle with depression significantly shapes the family's experience</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Memory and storytelling</td><td>Lucas's narration to his comatose daughter frames the entire novel</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Remember the frame narrative: the entire novel is Lucas telling his life story to his comatose daughter, Lucy, at her hospital bedside. This framing device is central to how the plot's flashback structure works.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Path of Lucas is an autobiographical Canadian novel told through Lucas Clarkson's narration to his comatose daughter, tracing his life of sacrifice and devotion to family through decades of hardship, including his wife's struggle with depression.\n</div>\n  ",
